# The box: margins between boxes do not add up, Margin: 0 auto centers a box, and a negative margin pulls it closer.
Document (dev.stxt.pdf):
	Language: en
	Title: The box · Margins
	Page:
		Paper: A4
		Margin: 20mm
	Styles:
		For style: demo
			Box:
				Padding: 6 8
				Background: tint
				Border: 0 0 0 2
				Border color: accent
	Section:
		Text: The box
			Style: topic
		Heading 1:
			Text: Margins
		Paragraph: The margin is the space outside the box, always transparent. Between two boxes one above the other, the vertical margins **do not add up**: the larger one is kept.
			Style: intro
		Text: Margin: 0 0 20 0  then  Margin: 30 0 0 0  (30 apart, not 50)
			Style: label
			Box:
				Margin: 0 0 6 0
		Text: Bottom margin 20.
			Style: demo
			Box:
				Margin: 0 0 20 0
		Text: Top margin 30.
			Style: demo
			Box:
				Margin: 30 0 0 0
		Text: Margin: 0 auto, with Width: 240  (centered)
			Style: label
			Box:
				Margin: 30 0 6 0
		Text: A centered box.
			Style: demo
			Box:
				Width: 240
				Margin: 0 auto
